  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5415",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to SW780 through a series of molecular interactions. The first pathway links Mollicellin N to A704, which is targeted by palmarumycin CP18, and then to SW780. The second pathway connects Mollicellin N to P2X purinoceptor 1, which is targeted by a compound that also targets SW780. The third pathway links Mollicellin N to TE-9, which is targeted by the same compound as in the second pathway and also targets SW780. These findings suggest that Mollicellin N may act through multiple pathways, potentially modulating different cellular processes that ultimately influence SW780. The evidence supports a mechanism where Mollicellin N exerts its effects via diverse molecular targets, which may converge on SW780 through shared downstream pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular interactions involved, emphasizing the importance of understanding the broader biological context in which these compounds operate.",
